# ELECTRA TPS Management System — Backend API

Build the complete backend API for managing 2,402 TPS (polling stations) across 12 districts in Kabupaten Sukoharjo for PAN.

## Existing Codebase

- **Laravel 13** with **Sanctum v4** auth already working
- User model with `HasApiTokens`, `SoftDeletes`, `#[Fillable]` attribute
- Existing patterns: thin controllers, Form Requests, API Resources, `fake()` in factories
- MySQL database (`octalectzz_tps-management`)
- Validation uses **string pipe notation** (existing convention)

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **New dependency required:** `maatwebsite/excel` must be installed via `composer require maatwebsite/excel` for the XLS import feature. This is a well-established Laravel package.

> [!WARNING]
> **Soft deletes on `tps` table only.** The user requested `destroy()` with soft delete on PollingStation. Other models use hard delete. Confirm this is intended.

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Response format:** The existing AuthController uses plain `response()->json()` without a consistent wrapper. The request asks for `{success, data, message, meta}` format. I'll introduce a `ApiResponse` trait on the base Controller to standardize this going forward without modifying existing auth endpoints.

> [!NOTE]
> **Table naming:** The request uses `tps` as the table name but `PollingStation` as the model. I'll use `polling_stations` as the table name following Laravel convention, with the model named `PollingStation`.

